{"step_index":403,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T18:11:11Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-24T23:41:11+05:30\nCompleted At: 2026-10-24T23:41:11+05:30\nShowing lines 1-50 of 157\n1: # HackerRank Orchestrate - October 2026\n2: \n3: ## Ghost Data Still Exists\n4: \n5: Build an AI agent that audits whether a user's personal data was actually deleted.\n6: \n7: A deletion workflow may report **Complete** while data still exists in databases, logs, support attachments, exports, search indexes, archives, or backups. Sync and restore processes may also bring deleted data back.\n8: \n9: For each request, the agent must first determine whether deletion was actually requested. It then returns `COMPLETE`, `INCOMPLETE`, or `NOT_APPLICABLE`, reports any remaining data or recreation risk, and produces the ordered remediation and verification steps required to finish an authorized deletion safely.\n10: \n11: Read [`problem_statement.md`](./problem_statement.md) for the complete challenge contract.\n12: \n13: ---\n14: \n15: ## Quick Start\n16: \n17: Clone the repository and move into the project directory:\n18: \n19: ```bash\n20: git clone https://github.com/interviewstreet/hackerrank-orchestrate-october26.git\n21: cd hackerrank-orchestrate-october26\n22: ```\n23: \n24: Start your AI coding tool from the **repository root** so it automatically reads [`AGENTS.md`](./AGENTS.md) and logs your session turns to `log.txt` in the root directory.\n25: \n26: Build your solution in `code/main.py`, or use another language and document its setup and run command clearly in your README.\n27: \n28: Your solution must:\n29: \n30: - Read the input files from `dataset/`\n31: - Generate one prediction row for every request in `dataset/deletion_requests.csv`\n32: - Write the final predictions to `output.csv` in the repository root\n33: \n34: Run the starter Python entry point with:\n35: \n36: ```bash\n37: python3 code/main.py\n38: ```\n39: \n40: The blank template at `dataset/output.csv` is provided as a reference. Your final generated file for submission must be the root-level `output.csv`.\n41: \n42: \n43: ## Dataset\n44: \n45: All participant-facing files are in `dataset/`:\n46: \n47: | File | Contents |\n48: | --- | --- |\n49: | `deletion_requests.csv` | 518 requests |\n50: | `sample_deletion_requests.csv` | 32 sample requests |"}
